1
00:00:00,880 --> 00:00:07,720
The Toy Maker

2
00:00:09,200 --> 00:00:19,560
Uncle Nhan makes toys from colorful dough.

3
00:00:20,360 --> 00:00:27,880
On street, wherever he goes stops where he goes children gather around.

4
00:00:28,560 --> 00:00:37,880
They look at toys, watch him make ducks, chickens,... all colors.

5
00:00:38,360 --> 00:00:50,160
One day, Uncle Nhan says he plans to go hometown to farm, not making toys anymore.

6
00:00:50,720 --> 00:00:53,440
I say:

7
00:00:53,920 --> 00:01:06,840
- Uncle don't go. Uncle stays here making toys to sell us.

8
00:01:07,880 --> 00:01:20,520
- These days many plastic toys, few people buy Uncle's toys.

9
00:01:21,800 --> 00:01:26,960
- I will buy and invite friends to buy too.

10
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:34,080
Uncle is moved hugs me.

11
00:01:34,800 --> 00:01:49,040
Next day, I break clay pig, ask classmates to help buy Uncle's toys.

12
00:01:51,040 --> 00:01:57,160
In afternoon, I see Uncle very happy.

13
00:01:57,560 --> 00:02:06,720
Uncle gives me two similar ones.

14
00:02:09,080 --> 00:02:12,840
Uncle tells me:

15
00:02:13,720 --> 00:02:23,080
Going back hometown, Uncle will also make toys to sell.

16
00:02:24,320 --> 00:02:37,160
Heard countryside children like this more than city children.

